## 2026-11-25 — PDF output via Chromium fallback

- User report: WebDoctor could not produce a PDF on this Windows machine. The earlier demo run skipped PDF with `cannot load library 'libgobject-2.0-0'`.
- Root cause: WeasyPrint raises `OSError` during module import when its native Pango/cairo libraries are missing. The previous `generate_pdf()` caught only `ImportError` around that import, so the exception escaped to the CLI instead of reaching the graceful fallback/skip path.
- Files: `webdoctor/reporters/pdf_report.py`, `tests/test_pdf_report.py`, `README.md`, `last changes`.
- Changes: split rendering into `_render_with_weasyprint()` and `_render_with_chromium()`. WeasyPrint remains the preferred renderer; native import failures and render failures are both caught. If WeasyPrint cannot produce a non-empty file, WebDoctor now falls back to headless Playwright Chromium (`page.set_content()` + `page.emulate_media("print")` + `page.pdf()` A4 with 12 mm margins). PDF generation returns `False` only when neither renderer produces a non-empty file. The README report table was updated to describe the fallback; the README test count was updated from 65 to 68. Tests now cover missing WeasyPrint, native-library import failure, broken WeasyPrint render, working WeasyPrint, missing Chromium output, and successful Chromium fallback. (CLI warning text was corrected in the 2026-11-25 accuracy/theme entry below.)
- Determinism note: byte-identical output remains guaranteed only for the WeasyPrint path; the Chromium fallback is best-effort and platform-dependent, but it renders the same HTML report content.
